# Reviewed effect classes of the library's string and formatting operations
# (docs/design/effects.md §3-4: reviewed primitive contracts, selected by
# resolved declaration identity: the bundled library file declaring the
# function, its name, and for formatting overloads the type each writes).
# Their bodies are runtime bookkeeping the inventory does not model (raw
# buffers, the allocator, refcounts), so a classified function's summary is its
# class, never its body. A string value is an immutable share: reading,
# passing or returning one copies nothing.
#
#   class               operations (Dewy spelling)
#   reads               text.length, is_empty, startswith, endswith, count,
#                       comparisons (=? <? ...), to_int(text max_digits=n)
#                       with a literal n from 1 to 18
#   allocates           interpolating text, a flag, a number or an `int`,
#                       trim, trim_start, trim_end, split, lines, join,
#                       replace, upper, lower, remove_prefix, remove_suffix,
#                       find, rfind, to_int (big results), `+ - *` on `int`,
#                       is_alpha, is_digit, is_space, is_alnum, set"..."
#   allocates, panics   indexing and slicing, byte_slice (each the caller's
#                       obligation where a direct call states it: its facts
#                       discharge it), find(part start), and a format
#                       specification unless a literal one the library
#                       accepts for the value (`{x:.2f}`)
#
# Anything else in the library is analyzed from its body. Demanded only by an
# effect summary: programs without rows never ask.
use 'ast.jo'
use 'util.jo'
use 'lex.jo'
use 'types.jo'
use 'check.jo'
use 'refine.jo'
use 'effects.jo'
use 'expr.jo'
use 'effect_classifiers.dewy'

enum EffectClass: unclassified, reads, allocates, allocates_panics

effect_class_cache: {int: EffectClass} = {}
# (the text members a program calls, `text.split(",")`: core/str.jo,
# std/graphemes.jo and std/dewy.jo)
effect_class_text: {int: bool} = {}
